  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDEA - Supporting Sudan&#x2019;s democratic transition</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IDEA - st&#xf6;d till Sudan&#xb4;s transition till demokrati</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektets &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att st&#xf6;dja den demokratiska &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ngen i Sudan genom att  uppr&#xe4;tta mekanismer f&#xf6;r dialog och konsensusuppbyggnad med fokus p&#xe5; delstatsniv&#xe5;; st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten f&#xf6;r NEC (National Election Committee) att leverera r&#xe4;ttvisa och fredliga val; &#xf6;ka kvinnors deltagande och representation i politiska processer;  samt st&#xe4;rka medborgarnas kunskap om politiska processer och  demokratiska styrning. Det f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas att Sudans &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ngsperiod och processer som initierats av transitionsregeringen kan leda till demokrati, men &#xe4;r i behov av kapasitetsst&#xe4;rkande &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder.   Projektet &#xe4;r  ett komplement till  EU&#xb4;s insats f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka demokrati i Sudan och som genomf&#xf6;rs av International IDEA.  Det &#xe4;r emellertid tv&#xe5; frist&#xe5;ende program. Programmet str&#xe4;cker sig &#xf6;ver tre &#xe5;r  (2020-2023) och budgeten &#xe4;r 45,3 MSEK</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective is to support the democratic transition of Sudan by supporting the establishment of mechanisms for dialogue and consensus-building on the transition processes; strengthen the capacity of NEC (National Election Committee)  deliver credible and peaceful elections; enhance women participation and representation in political processes, and strengthen citizens awareness on the transitional processes and the broader democratic governance practices. It is anticipated that Sudan&#x2019;s transition period and processes will provide an opportunity for the country&#x2019;s transition to democracy. The contribution is a complement to EU&#xb4;s project for strengthening democracy in Sudan and is implemented by International IDEA. The project is complementary to the EU&#xb4;s contribution to strengthening the democracy in Sudan and is implemented by IDEA. However, they are two independent projects.   The duration of the project is 2020-2023, and the total budget is 45,3 MSEK.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall purpose of the contribution was to support Sudans transition to a democratic system.

The objectives of the contribution were to contribute to the following:

- Improved citizens awareness on transitional processes and democratic governance.

- Policymakers within political parties and the government apply increased knowledge and skills to make more informed choices regarding democracy reforms.

- The National Election Commission apply increased knowledge and skills to recognize and respond to complexities and risks in the electoral processes and effectively implement the Electoral Cycle Approach.

- Civil society (with a focus on womens groups) and media in Sudan apply increased knowledge and skills to engage with constitution-makers, policymakers in political parties and government and the National Election Commission democratically and effectively and promote broad public participation in the process.

After the military coup in October, 2021 the objectives of the intervention were revised and technical assistance to the government or its institutions was halted. The revised programme focused on:

- Training and strengthening civil society on democratic issues with a focus on young people and women, and

- Cooperating with other organisations to resist the closure of civil society.

- Continued support to women&apos;s political participation and an assessment of the framework for disabled persons&apos; opportunities to participate in elections.

After the civil war broke out in 2023, all activities focusing on electoral issues were cancelled. Instead IDEA focused on strengthening the expertise of various parties and organisations on the links between peace and democratic governance and to enhance women&apos;s political participation at all levels.</narrative>
  </description>
